d a few friends that's  already took their own path but they're  finally guiding their way back  and a lot of people getting the  unemployment i know i understand that it  helps them  but sometimes they just want to buy  other stuff with it  how bad does it get in high school  there's how serious is the drug problem  i mean  they even get to where they bring it to  school and sell it  it's bad  and their families have the same  situation you you do  it's in their family so that's what  they've it's the role models they've had  what's been your favorite memory in your  16 years  having my little niece and nephew around  yeah you have a couple  small you have a sister and a niece that  um i have a niece and a nephew  or a nephew yeah and lisa's your  she's my niece my oldest sister had her  and her little brother brayden and  her mother took the same path as  our real mother because she wanted her  attention so bad when she was little  so your mom kind of takes care of  you your niece and my nephew and your  nephew and you guys are all  obviously drug free and yeah and  avoiding everyone that is  yeah who's using right good for you  so what are the best and worst things  about living in appalachia  the good thing is like the scenery  that you can see all over like the fall  and i say about the only bad thing about  around here is  the drug usage and all that like  young kids to adults  can you can you even envision staying  here and trying to find a job and all  that  it's just hopeless it's just helpless  yeah  it's a shame because it's such a lovely  part of the country yeah  but it's just been destroyed yeah it's a  lack of employment in the drugs  and your mom must be very proud yeah  she's  very ecstatic with me yeah  and what what so what i'm like you see  people in your family i mean what  they going through like depression and  jail time and  all kinds of stuff like this right yeah  so that's such a great warning sign for  you just to  just stare clear that's 